Chapter: Maybe

 We say:

Section: Definitions

  Maybe (a) =
    | Just (a)
    | None

  from-maybe : Maybe a, a -> a
  from-maybe (m) (default) = when m
    is Just (x) -> x
    is None -> default

  is-just : Maybe a -> Boolean
  is-just (m) = when m
    is Just (x) -> True
    is None -> False

  is-none : Maybe a -> Boolean
  is-none (m) = when m
    is Just (x) -> False
    is None -> True

  maybe-map : (a -> b), Maybe a -> Maybe b
  maybe-map (f) (m) = when m
    is Just (x) -> Just (f x)
    is None -> None

  maybe-bind : Maybe a, (a -> Maybe b) -> Maybe b
  maybe-bind (m) (f) = when m
    is Just (x) -> f x
    is None -> None

Page 1

Chapter: Collate

 Collation is not encoding, and this chapter exists so the two cannot be
 mistaken for each other.

 Three orders exist in Codex and each has its own name. Identity is `==`,
 which asks whether two texts are the same. Encoding order is
 `text-compare`, which is fast, total and consistent, and is what an
 ordered container wants; it ranks by CCE code point, and CCE numbers the
 letters by English frequency, so `d` comes before `b` and `t` before `a`.
 Collation is this chapter: the order a human reads, where `b` comes
 before `d` and `zebra` comes after `Apple`. Both of those are the other
 way round in encoding order, the second because CCE's lowercase band
 sits entirely below its uppercase band, so `z` at 38 outranks `A` at 41.

 The ordering operators are refused on Text and on Char precisely so that
 neither of the other two can impersonate this one.

Section: What a key is

Section: The bands and their weights

 CCE tier 0 is laid out in bands: whitespace 0-2, digits 3-12, lowercase
 13-38, uppercase 39-64, punctuation 65-96, accented Latin 97-112,
 Cyrillic 113-127. The weights below place whitespace first, then
 punctuation, then digits in numeric order, then the Latin letters in
 alphabetical order with both cases and every accented form folded onto
 the same weight, then Cyrillic.

  collate-weight-space : Integer = 1
  collate-weight-punct : Integer = 4
  collate-weight-digit : Integer = 36
  collate-weight-latin : Integer = 46
  collate-weight-cyrillic : Integer = 72
  collate-weight-other : Integer = 100

 CCE orders the lowercase letters by English frequency:
 e t a o i n s h r d l c u m w f g y p b v k j x q z. This table is the
 alphabetical index of each of them, in that order, so entry 0 is 4
 because `e` is the fifth letter of the alphabet. The uppercase band at
 39-64 carries the same letters in the same order and reuses it.

 A table that restates an encoding is the kind of thing that drifts away
 from what it describes, so `codex/test/collate-order` checks every entry
 against `to-unicode`, which is the mapping CCE itself publishes. A test
 can afford that call once per character; a comparison loop cannot, which
 is why the table is here at all.

  collate-alpha-index : List Integer
  collate-alpha-index = [4, 19, 0, 14, 8, 13, 18, 7, 17, 3, 11, 2, 20,
                         12, 22, 5, 6, 24, 15, 1, 21, 10, 9, 23, 16, 25]

 The sixteen accented forms at 97-112 are e-acute, e-grave, e-circumflex,
 e-diaeresis, a-acute, a-grave, a-circumflex, a-diaeresis, o-acute,
 o-circumflex, o-diaeresis, u-acute, u-diaeresis, n-tilde, c-cedilla and
 i-acute. This table is the alphabetical index of each one's BASE letter,
 which is what folding an accent means.

  collate-accent-base : List Integer
  collate-accent-base = [4, 4, 4, 4, 0, 0, 0, 0, 14, 14, 14, 20, 20, 13, 2, 8]

Section: Weighing one character

 Both tables are parameters rather than names inside the loop. A list
 constant is a definition and not storage, so naming one at a recursion
 site re-materialises the whole thing on every character; `CCE.codex`
 documents that in its own prose about `from-unicode-tier0` and this is
 the same shape.

  collate-primary : List Integer, List Integer, Integer -> Integer
  collate-primary (alpha) (accents) (cp) =
    if cp < 3 then collate-weight-space + cp
    else if cp < 13 then collate-weight-digit + (cp - 3)
    else if cp < 39 then collate-weight-latin + list-at alpha (cp - 13)
    else if cp < 65 then collate-weight-latin + list-at alpha (cp - 39)
    else if cp < 97 then collate-weight-punct + (cp - 65)
    else if cp < 113 then collate-weight-latin + list-at accents (cp - 97)
    else if cp < 128 then collate-weight-cyrillic + (cp - 113)
    else collate-weight-other

  collate-secondary : Integer -> Integer
  collate-secondary (cp) =
    if cp < 39 then 1
    else if cp < 65 then 2
    else if cp < 97 then 1
    else if cp < 113 then 3 + (cp - 97)
    else 1

Section: Building the key

  collate-char : Integer -> Text
  collate-char (cp) = char-to-text (code-to-char cp)

  collate-key : Text -> Text
  collate-key (s) =
    let n = text-length s
    in let primaries = collate-primary-run collate-alpha-index collate-accent-base s 0 n ""
    in let seconds = collate-secondary-run s 0 n ""
    in primaries & collate-char 0 & seconds

  collate-primary-run : List Integer, List Integer, Text, Integer, Integer, Text -> Text
  collate-primary-run (alpha) (accents) (s) (i) (n) (out) =
    if i >= n then out
    else let w = collate-char (collate-primary alpha accents (char-code-at s i))
    in collate-primary-run alpha accents s (i + 1) n (out & w)

  collate-secondary-run : Text, Integer, Integer, Text -> Text
  collate-secondary-run (s) (i) (n) (out) =
    if i >= n then out
    else let w = collate-char (collate-secondary (char-code-at s i))
    in collate-secondary-run s (i + 1) n (out & w)

  text-collate : Text, Text -> Integer
  text-collate (a) (b) = text-compare (collate-key a) (collate-key b)

Section: What this is not

 This is Codex collation: one deterministic, locale-free order, and an
 approximation rather than a claim of correctness for any language.
 Swedish files o-diaeresis after z and German files it with o, and both
 are right; neither is what this does. A locale-tailored order, if it is
 ever wanted, arrives as a parameter to `collate-key` and never as a
 change to what the default answers.

Chapter: SecretEntry
  cites Foreword chapter Maybe
  cites Foreword chapter ListUtils
  cites Foreword chapter Collate

Section: Entry Types

  SecretType =
    | SecretPassword
    | SecretApiKey
    | SecretToken
    | SecretCertificate
    | SecretNote
    | SecretSshKey
    | SecretDatabase
    | SecretWifi
    | SecretCreditCard
    | SecretIdentity

Section: Core Record

  SecretEntry = record {
    se-id          : Integer,
    se-type        : SecretType,
    se-name        : Text,
    se-username    : Text,
    se-url         : Text,
    se-tags        : List Text,
    se-folder      : Text,
    se-notes       : Text,
    se-created     : Integer,
    se-modified    : Integer,
    se-accessed    : Integer,
    se-access-count : Integer,
    se-favorite    : Boolean,
    se-archived    : Boolean
  }

  SecretPayload = record {
    sp-password     : Text,
    sp-fields       : List SecretField,
    sp-totp-secret  : Text,
    sp-attachments  : List AttachmentRef
  }

  SecretField = record {
    sf-name    : Text,
    sf-value   : Text,
    sf-hidden  : Boolean
  }

  AttachmentRef = record {
    ar-name : Text,
    ar-size : Integer,
    ar-hash : List Integer
  }

Section: Encrypted Form

  EncryptedSecret = record {
    es-id       : Integer,
    es-metadata : SecretEntry,
    es-nonce    : List Integer,
    es-cipher   : List Integer,
    es-tag      : List Integer
  }

Section: Construction

  secret-new : Integer, SecretType, Text, Text, Text, Integer -> SecretEntry
  secret-new (id) (stype) (name) (username) (url) (now) =
    SecretEntry {
      se-id = id,
      se-type = stype,
      se-name = name,
      se-username = username,
      se-url = url,
      se-tags = [],
      se-folder = "Default",
      se-notes = "",
      se-created = now,
      se-modified = now,
      se-accessed = now,
      se-access-count = 0,
      se-favorite = False,
      se-archived = False
    }

  payload-new : Text -> SecretPayload
  payload-new (password) =
    SecretPayload {
      sp-password = password,
      sp-fields = [],
      sp-totp-secret = "",
      sp-attachments = []
    }

  payload-with-fields : Text, List SecretField -> SecretPayload
  payload-with-fields (password) (fields) =
    SecretPayload {
      sp-password = password,
      sp-fields = fields,
      sp-totp-secret = "",
      sp-attachments = []
    }

Section: Field Helpers

  field-new : Text, Text, Boolean -> SecretField
  field-new (name) (value) (hidden) =
    SecretField { sf-name = name, sf-value = value, sf-hidden = hidden }

  field-visible : Text, Text -> SecretField
  field-visible (name) (value) =
    field-new name value False

  field-hidden : Text, Text -> SecretField
  field-hidden (name) (value) =
    field-new name value True

Section: Entry Updates

  secret-touch : SecretEntry, Integer -> SecretEntry
  secret-touch (se) (now) =
    let se1 = __record-set se "se-accessed" now
    in __record-set se1 "se-access-count" (se.se-access-count + 1)

  secret-modify : SecretEntry, Integer -> SecretEntry
  secret-modify (se) (now) =
    __record-set (secret-touch se now) "se-modified" now

  secret-set-folder : SecretEntry, Text -> SecretEntry
  secret-set-folder (se) (folder) =
    __record-set se "se-folder" folder

  secret-set-tags : SecretEntry, List Text -> SecretEntry
  secret-set-tags (se) (tags) =
    __record-set se "se-tags" tags

  secret-add-tag : SecretEntry, Text -> SecretEntry
  secret-add-tag (se) (tag) =
    __record-set se "se-tags" (list-push se.se-tags tag)

  secret-toggle-favorite : SecretEntry -> SecretEntry
  secret-toggle-favorite (se) =
    __record-set se "se-favorite" (if se.se-favorite then False else True)

  secret-archive : SecretEntry -> SecretEntry
  secret-archive (se) =
    __record-set se "se-archived" True

  secret-unarchive : SecretEntry -> SecretEntry
  secret-unarchive (se) =
    __record-set se "se-archived" False

Section: Type Names

  secret-type-name : SecretType -> Text
  secret-type-name (st) =
    when st
      is SecretPassword -> "Password"
      is SecretApiKey -> "API Key"
      is SecretToken -> "Token"
      is SecretCertificate -> "Certificate"
      is SecretNote -> "Secure Note"
      is SecretSshKey -> "SSH Key"
      is SecretDatabase -> "Database"
      is SecretWifi -> "Wi-Fi"
      is SecretCreditCard -> "Credit Card"
      is SecretIdentity -> "Identity"

  secret-type-icon : SecretType -> Text
  secret-type-icon (st) =
    when st
      is SecretPassword -> "[P]"
      is SecretApiKey -> "[K]"
      is SecretToken -> "[T]"
      is SecretCertificate -> "[C]"
      is SecretNote -> "[N]"
      is SecretSshKey -> "[S]"
      is SecretDatabase -> "[D]"
      is SecretWifi -> "[W]"
      is SecretCreditCard -> "[$]"
      is SecretIdentity -> "[I]"

Section: Search

  secret-matches : SecretEntry, Text -> Boolean
  secret-matches (se) (query) =
    if text-length query == 0 then True
    else text-contains se.se-name query
      | text-contains se.se-username query
      | text-contains se.se-url query
      | tags-match se.se-tags query

  tags-match : List Text, Text -> Boolean
  tags-match (tags) (query) =
    if list-length tags == 0 then False
    else if text-contains (list-at tags 0) query then True
      else tags-match (list-drop tags 1) query

Section: Sorting

  secret-sort-name : SecretEntry, SecretEntry -> Boolean
  secret-sort-name (a) (b) = text-collate a.se-name b.se-name < 0

  secret-sort-modified : SecretEntry, SecretEntry -> Boolean
  secret-sort-modified (a) (b) = a.se-modified > b.se-modified

  secret-sort-accessed : SecretEntry, SecretEntry -> Boolean
  secret-sort-accessed (a) (b) = a.se-accessed > b.se-accessed

Chapter: Console

 We say:

Section: Definitions

  effect Console where
    print-line-uni : Text -> [Console.Write] Nothing
    read-line  : [Console.Read] Text

